{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562557-vampire-dark-ages-advice-or-suggestions-for-ritual","id":1562557,"title":"Vampire Dark Ages advice or suggestions for Ritual","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-03T08:06:38-07:00","id":1562557,"title":"Vampire Dark Ages advice or suggestions for Ritual","content":"I\u2019m struggling to create a balanced necromancy ritual, that is in theme with a ritual or combination discipline \u201cBeasts Vigour\u201d that transfers wounds to a ghoul.<br /> i am trying to come up with an alternate, that transfers wounds to a Wraith/Ghost/Drone.<br /> I had considered possibly changing it to animated corpses.<br /> <br /> Could anyone assist or make suggestions on how to write up this up as a more balanced ritual? <br /> I either end up with a ritual that has too many negatives or too many positives with very few negatives.<br /> <br /> thanks in advance to all who are helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:10:32-07:00","id":1562596,"title":"","content":"Hard to say without first seeing what are you coming up with.<br /> <br /> Bad or worse, show your prototypes and what you think of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:22:46-07:00","id":1562598,"title":"","content":"I think the balance is going to be difficult to establish because it really depends on how much a given ST stresses the costs of cultivating and maintaining loyal ghouls. If the ST makes having a squad of low key ghouls that hang around just to be wound-batteries for you, it shouldn't be that hard to put the same on ghosts without much effort. If ghouls take a lot of work, foisting damage onto them becomes more costly and &quot;balance&quot; would indicate that doing the same to ghosts should take equivalently more effort.<br /> <br /> So generally this results in two main approaches you get stuck with: Either ignore Beast's Vigor beyond conceptual basis and try to make what feels like a decent Necromancy ritual based on what Necromancy can do, or design the mechanic with some sort of sliding scale of costs that the ST can use to adjust the ritual's costs to be in-line with similar effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:37:09-07:00","id":1562601,"title":"","content":"I felt like I should give an example of what I mean by a sliding scale option after I hit post and did something else for a few minutes:<br /> <br /> Something the Necromancy ritual could do is harm a Fetter instead of just doing damage to the ghost itself. Acquiring Fetters, how much damage a given Fetter can take, and how much this becomes a problem with angry ghosts, put it in the subjective ST controlled space as ghoul management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T02:35:41-07:00","id":1562621,"title":"","content":"Without additional context, I would sketch it out like this:<br /> <br /> Algea's Coffin (Level Three)<br /> <br /> In a container of bone or ivory create a bed of dried mistletoe leaves. Put three drops of your vitae on the leaves, then place a Fetter on them and seal the container with beeswax.<br /> <br /> Until sunrise any harm done to the necromancer will be transferred to the Wraith. At dawn, all damage returns to the caster as Bashing damage, which may be soaked. Should the damage exceed the Corpus levels of the Wraith or the seal be undone, the Fetter breaks and all damage returns immediately.<br /> <br /> I liked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>' idea of possibly breaking the Fetter, it's a good incentive to be not too careless about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:35:16-07:00","id":1562659,"title":"","content":"I have problems with my short term memory, and i lose (misplace) notes.<br /> i had totally overlooked and/or forgotten about fetters!<br /> <br /> my character cannot sire, blood bond, or create ghouls.<br /> I was fixating on trying a work-around for that part, and mostly trying to merge the two rituals (creating an undead servant, with Beast Vigor) and getting frustrated, then forgetting key details.<br /> <br /> Also been trying to read Wraith corebook, but feel like i\u2019m getting more confused and mixed-up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:51:30-07:00","id":1562663,"title":"","content":"Unless your table plans on using the Wraith rules for ghosts, I would really suggest saving that for another time. Wraith can get pretty dense since it's the most detached from the mortal world of the WoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}